# Riverchurn Monument against Bot2's Leyline of the Void ("If a card would be put into an opponent's graveyard from
# anywhere, exile it instead"). On turn 3 Bot1's "{1}, {T}: Any number of target players each mill two cards" targets
# both players: Bot1's two cards are exiled instead (CR 614.1a, 701.17c) and Bot2's two reach Bot2's graveyard, in the
# one mill. On turn 5 the exhaust ("each mill cards equal to the number of cards in their graveyard") targets both
# again: Bot1's graveyard is empty, so Bot1 mills none - the count is the graveyard's, not the cards milled before -
# and Bot2 mills two.

